  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through Friday)\nIssued at 200 AM CST Sat Nov 7 2026\n\nWarm, above-normal temperatures will continue on Tuesday and \nWednesday with highs generally in the 70s and lows generally in \nthe upper 40s and 50s deg F. Bias-corrected probabilistic guidance\nindicates little spread during these two days, which indicates \nhigh confidence that the relatively warm weather will continue.\n\nBy Thursday into Friday, ensemble spread increases markedly as a \ncold front will likely move across the Southern Plains as a \nlongwave trough develops across the eastern half of the United \nStates. This pattern will allow a cold front to drive southward as\nthe trough amplifies to the east. \n\nWith the Southern Plains southwest of the strongest cold air \nadvection, there is uncertainty regarding how much cold air will \nadvance into Oklahoma and north Texas. It will be highly dependent\non the track of the attendant surface high behind the cold front.\nBias-corrected probabilistic guidance indicates a ~20 to 30 deg F\nspread between the 10th and 90th percentiles with a 20 to 40% \nchance of high temperatures below 60 deg F by next Friday.\n\nMahale",
